<title>CHILE: Chile's CMPC studies new plant - report.</title>
<headline>Chile's CMPC studies new plant - report.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean paper producer Empresas CMPC is studying building an $800 million plant which would produce 400,000 tonnes of wood pulp a year, reported newspaper El Mercurio Wednesday.</p>
<p>The newspaper, quoting the firm's secretary general Gonzalo Garcia, said CMPC plans to bring the plant into operation by the end of the decade.</p>
<p>The company is also building a $215 million cardboard plant which will produce 130,000 tonnes of board when it comes on line in early 1998, Garcia was quoted as saying.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
